  <dashboards>
    <dashboard name='1 Activity and Calories'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='900' maxwidth='1400' minheight='900' minwidth='1400' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='109' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'><zone h='100000' id='108' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='100000' x='0' y='0'><zone h='9000' id='100' type-v2='text' w='100000' x='0' y='0'><formatted-text><run bold='true' fontsize='16'>Bellabeat: what drives calories burned?</run><run>Æ&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#52514e' fontsize='10'>33 Fitbit users, Apr 12 - May 12 2016 (850 clean user-days). Intensity matters more than step count: 10k+ step days burn 44% more calories than &lt;5k days, with ~50 very active minutes vs 3.</run></formatted-text></zone><zone h='45500' id='104' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='100000' x='0' y='9000'><zone h='45500' id='101' name='Avg calories burned per day, by daily steps' w='34000' x='0' y='9000' /><zone h='45500' id='102' name='Avg very active minutes per day, by daily steps' w='33000' x='34000' y='9000' /><zone h='45500' id='103' name='Correlation with calories, within the same user (r)' w='33000' x='67000' y='9000' /></zone><zone h='45500' id='107' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='100000' x='0' y='54500'><zone h='45500' id='105' name='Avg steps by hour of day: peaks at lunch and after work' w='60000' x='0' y='54500' /><zone h='45500' id='106' name='Avg steps by weekday: Sunday is lowest' w='40000' x='60000' y='54500' /></zone></zone></zone>
      </zones>
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard name='2 Sleep and Engagement'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='900' maxwidth='1400' minheight='900' minwidth='1400' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='117' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'><zone h='100000' id='116' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='100000' x='0' y='0'><zone h='9000' id='110' type-v2='text' w='100000' x='0' y='0'><formatted-text><run bold='true' fontsize='16'>Bellabeat: sleep and device engagement</run><run>Æ&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#52514e' fontsize='10'>24 users logged 398 nights; only 55% reached 7h. 9 of 33 users never logged sleep. Sedentary share of awake time is used because raw sedentary minutes shrink mechanically with time in bed.</run></formatted-text></zone><zone h='45500' id='112' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='100000' x='0' y='9000'><zone h='45500' id='111' name='Nights with 7h+ sleep, by sedentary share of awake time' w='100000' x='0' y='9000' /></zone><zone h='45500' id='115' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='100000' x='0' y='54500'><zone h='45500' id='113' name='Users by how often they logged sleep (of 33)' w='50000' x='0' y='54500' /><zone h='45500' id='114' name='Users by days the tracker was worn (of 31)' w='50000' x='50000' y='54500' /></zone></zone></zone>
      </zones>
    </dashboard>
